{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@discardableResult","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"insert","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"edge","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedEdgeV","text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedEdge"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:26DirectedAcyclicGraphModule0abC0V","text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:26DirectedAcyclicGraphModule0B9EdgeErrorO","text":"AcyclicEdgeError","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/AcyclicEdgeError"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:26DirectedAcyclicGraphModule0abC0V","text":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The edge’s position: a new one, or on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AdjacencyList"},{"type":"text","text":", which is simple, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"existing edge’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When the source is already placed before the target, the cost is two array reads plus the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"base’s insertion. Otherwise Pearce and Kelly’s reordering runs, O(‖δ‖ + δ log δ) for the δ","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices it visits between the endpoints’ places; see the type’s documentation. A rejection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allocates nothing once the reordering’s scratch has grown.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Throws","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"AcyclicEdgeError.selfLoop","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a self-loop, and ","type":"text"},{"code":".cycle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when the edge would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"close a cycle; then nothing changes, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"bidirectionalShortestPath(from: edge.target, to: edge.source)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Traversal) is a path the edge would close. ","type":"text"},{"code":"try?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" turns a rejection","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"type":"aside"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/DirectedAcyclicGraph\/insert(edge:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule","doc:\/\/DirectedAcyclicGraphModule\/documentation\